msgstr "Guided night turtle tour"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1880
msgid "El tortuguero se observa con guía: no se puede alterar la anidación."
msgstr "The turtles are watched with a guide: nesting cannot be disturbed."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1881
msgid "Hay corrientes fuertes en la playa: nade con cuidado"
msgstr "There are strong currents in the beach: swim with care"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1882
msgid "Use repelente en la zona de manglar"
msgstr "Use repellent in the mangrove area"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1884
msgid ""
"Protege una de las últimas poblaciones de tortuga baula del Caribe, junto "
"con el manglar más extenso de la zona."
msgstr ""
"It protects one of the last leatherback turtle populations in the Caribbean, "
"together with the largest mangrove in the area."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1909
msgid ""
"Niebla constante, aves que viven en el dosel y uno de los hábitats más "
"difíciles de conservar del planeta."
msgstr ""
"Constant fog, birds that live in the canopy and one of the hardest habitats "
"on the planet to conserve."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1911
msgid ""
"La neblina cubre el bosque casi todo el año y mantiene la humedad que lo "
"hace único."
msgstr ""
"The mist covers the forest almost all year round and keeps the humidity that "
"makes it unique."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1912
msgid ""
"El quetzal anida en las copas: el macho tiene una cola de hasta un metro."
msgstr ""
"The quetzal nests in the treetops: the male has a tail up to one meter long."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1913
msgid ""
"Protege 1.600 hectáreas donde las epífitas cubren el 75 por ciento de los "
"troncos."
msgstr ""
"It protects 1,600 hectares where epiphytes cover 75 percent of the trunks."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1914
msgid "Se recorre con senderos de tablones y pasarelas entre la neblina."
msgstr "It is explored along boardwalk trails and walkways through the mist."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1917
msgid "Quetzal, la cotinga y el tucán del bosque nuboso"
msgstr "Quetzal, cotinga and toucan of the cloud forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1918
msgid "Gavilanes, tucanes y más de 400 especies de aves"
msgstr "Hawks, toucans and more than 400 bird species"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1919
msgid "Perezoso de dos dedos, armadillo y zarigueya"
msgstr "Two-toed sloth, armadillo and opossum"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1920
msgid "Ranitas de colores y orquídeas epífitas"
msgstr "Colorful little frogs and epiphytic orchids"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1923
msgid "Recorrido guiado por los senderos con pasarela"
msgstr "Guided tour along the boardwalk trails"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1924
msgid "Avistamiento del quetzal en los árboles"
msgstr "Quetzal sighting in the trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1925
msgid "Caminatas nocturnas para ver animales activos"
msgstr "Night walks to spot active wildlife"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1926
msgid "Visita al centro de visitantes del bosque"
msgstr "Visit to the forest visitor center"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1929
msgid "Lleve ropa impermeable y calzado cómodo"
msgstr "Bring waterproof clothing and comfortable shoes"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1930
msgid "El sendero puede resbalar con la humedad"
msgstr "The trail can be slippery when wet"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1931
msgid "Use repelente y linterna"
msgstr "Use insect repellent and a flashlight"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1933
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:1975
msgid "Todos los días, de 7:00 a 16:00"
msgstr "Every day, 7:00 to 16:00"

