msgstr "Visit to the nearby beaches"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2265
msgid "El sol es fuerte y no hay sombra en el camino."
msgstr "The sun is strong and there is no shade on the path."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2266
msgid "Los caminos son rocosos, use calzado firme."
msgstr "The paths are rocky, wear sturdy footwear."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2267
msgid "El bosque seco es ralo: no espere sombra."
msgstr "The dry forest is sparse: do not expect shade."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2269
msgid "Acceso libre todo el día en las áreas publicas"
msgstr "Open access all day in the public areas"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2270
msgid "Sin entrada a las playas"
msgstr "No entry fee for the beaches"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2271
msgid "Cabo, Playa Nacascolo y los acantilados del norte"
msgstr "Cape, Playa Nacascolo and the northern cliffs"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2272
msgid "2008"
msgstr "2008"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2274
msgid "Bosque seco tropical, manglar y costa rocosa"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest, mangrove and rocky coast"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2275
msgid "0-80 msnm"
msgstr "0-80 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2277
msgid ""
"El cabo pertenece al Área de Conservación Tempisque, que protege el bosque "
"seco y la anidación de tortugas."
msgstr ""
"The cape belongs to the Tempisque Conservation Area, which protects the dry "
"forest and turtle nesting."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2278
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2631
msgid ""
"Se llega en vehículo por camino de tierra; el sendero al acantilado es de "
"rocas."
msgstr "You arrive by vehicle on a dirt road; the trail to the cliff is rocky."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2280
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2630
msgid ""
"Cabo Papagayo marca el punto más septentrional de la península de Nicoya. El "
"camino costero pasa entre bosque seco y acantilados hasta el mirador del "
"golfo. Alrededor hay hoteles y playas, y al sur el refugio de tortugas de "
"Ostional."
msgstr ""
"Cabo Papagayo marks the northernmost point of the Nicoya Peninsula. The "
"coastal road passes between dry forest and cliffs up to the gulf lookout. "
"Around it there are hotels and beaches, and to the south the Ostional turtle "
"sanctuary."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2287
msgid ""
"El punto más alto de la sierra de Talamanca, con vista al valle de Savegre."
msgstr ""
"The highest point of the Talamanca range, with views over the Savegre Valley."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2289
msgid "Su cima llega a 3.642 msnm y se conoce también como Savegre."
msgstr "Its summit reaches 3.642 masl and is also known as Savegre."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2290
msgid "La carretera interamericana pasa a poca distancia del mirador."
msgstr "The Inter-American Highway passes close to the lookout."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2291
msgid "Desde el mirador se ve el valle de Savegre y el Pacífico."
msgstr "From the lookout you can see the Savegre Valley and the Pacific."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2292
msgid "Alrededor hay plantaciones de pino, páramo y bosque frío de montaña."
msgstr "Around there are pine plantations, páramo and cold montane forest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2295
msgid "Gallo de monte, ave endémica de la sierra"
msgstr "Wild turkey, endemic bird of the range"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2296
msgid "Quetzal resplandeciente en el bosque nuboso cercano"
msgstr "Resplendent quetzal in the nearby cloud forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2297
msgid "Mono aullador en las zonas más bajas"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the lower areas"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2298
msgid "Tapir de monte, el mamífero mayor del país"
msgstr "Mountain tapir, the largest mammal in the country"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2301
msgid "Caminata por el mirador de la carretera"
msgstr "Walk at the highway lookout"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2302
msgid "Visita a la Reserva Biológica Lomas Barbudal, muy cerca"
msgstr "Visit to Lomas Barbudal Biological Reserve, very close by"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2303
msgid "Recorrido por fincas de café y miel en el valle"
msgstr "Tour of the coffee and honey farms in the valley"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2304
msgid "Fotografía del valle al amanecer"
msgstr "Photography of the valley at dawn"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2307
msgid "Arriba hace frío y viento casi todo el año."
msgstr "It is cold and windy up top almost all year."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2308
msgid "En la mañana hay neblina y la vista se pierde."
msgstr "In the morning there is mist and the view disappears."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2309
msgid "En temporada de lluvias use un vehículo 4x4."
msgstr "In the rainy season use a 4x4 vehicle."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2311
msgid "Acceso todo el día; la carretera permanece abierta todo el año"
msgstr "Open all day; the road stays open all year"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2313
msgid "Mirador y tramo de la ruta 32 en la sierra de Talamanca"
msgstr "Lookout and stretch of Route 32 in the Talamanca range"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2314
msgid "1943"
msgstr "1943"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2315
msgid "Talamanca"
msgstr "Talamanca"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2316
msgid "Páramo de alta altura, bosque de pino y bosque nuboso"
msgstr "High-altitude páramo, pine forest and cloud forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2317
msgid "1.500-3.642 msnm"
msgstr "1.500-3.642 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2318
msgid "Diciembre a abril, y julio para la carretera"
msgstr "December to April, and July for the road"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2319
msgid ""
"Protege el pino, el páramo y el bosque nuboso de la sierra de Talamanca."
msgstr ""
"It protects the pine trees, the páramo and the cloud forest of the Talamanca "
"range."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2320
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2636
msgid "Llega en vehículo por la ruta 32; el mirador no tiene rampa."
msgstr "Get there by vehicle on Route 32; the lookout has no ramp."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2322
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2635
msgid ""
"A 3.642 msnm está la cima más alta de la sierra de Talamanca. La carretera "
"interamericana que cruza el cerro se completó en 1943. Desde el mirador se "
"ve el valle de Savegre y el mar en días claros."
msgstr ""
"At 3.642 masl lies the highest summit of the Talamanca range. The Inter-"
"American Highway crossing the mountain was completed in 1943. From the "
"lookout you can see the Savegre Valley and the sea on clear days."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2329
msgid ""
"La península más grande del país: bosque seco al norte y selva húmeda al sur."
msgstr ""
"The largest peninsula in the country: dry forest in the north and rainforest "
"in the south."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2331
msgid "La península mide unos 3.200 km² y es la más grande del país."
msgstr "The peninsula covers some 3.200 km² and is the largest in the country."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2332
msgid "El norte es bosque seco y el sur es selva húmeda."
msgstr "The north is dry forest and the south is rainforest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2333
msgid "El Área de Conservación Guanacaste fue creada en 1991."
msgstr "The Guanacaste Conservation Area was created in 1991."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2334
msgid "Allí están Santa Rosa, Palo Verde y el río Tempisque."
msgstr "Santa Rosa, Palo Verde and the Tempisque River are located there."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2337
msgid "Venado cola blanca en el bosque seco"
msgstr "White-tailed deer in the dry forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2338
msgid "Mono aullador en la selva del sur"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the southern rainforest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2339
msgid "Tortuga verde en las playas del Golfo de Nicoya"
msgstr "Green turtle on the beaches of the Gulf of Nicoya"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2340
msgid "Ara escarlata en los árboles del bosque seco"
msgstr "Scarlet macaw in the dry forest trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2343
msgid "Visita a las áreas protegidas de la península"
msgstr "Visit to the protected areas of the peninsula"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2344
msgid "Paseo en bote por el río Tempisque"
msgstr "Boat ride along the Tempisque River"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2345
msgid "Visita a los pueblos pesqueros del sur"
msgstr "Visit to the southern fishing towns"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2346
msgid "Recorrido por el cabo y sus miradores"
msgstr "Tour of the cape and its lookouts"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2349
msgid "Las distancias entre los extremos de la península son largas."
msgstr "Distances between the ends of the peninsula are long."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2350
msgid "El sur es muy lluvioso en temporada."
msgstr "The south is very rainy in season."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2351
msgid "Planifique la ruta con un mapa antes de salir."
msgstr "Plan your route with a map before setting out."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2353
msgid "Acceso libre todo el día; cada reserva cobra su entrada"
msgstr "Open access all day; each reserve charges its own fee"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2354
msgid "Sin entrada general; cada reserva protegida tiene la suya"
msgstr "No general entry fee; each protected reserve has its own"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2355
msgid "Península de 3.200 km² con áreas protegidas de todo tipo"
msgstr "A 3.200 km² peninsula with protected areas of every kind"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2358
msgid "Del bosque seco tropical a la selva húmeda"
msgstr "From tropical dry forest to rainforest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2359
msgid "0-1.200 msnm"
msgstr "0-1.200 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2360
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2402
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2444
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2486
msgid "Diciembre a abril"
msgstr "December to April"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2361
msgid ""
"El Área de Conservación Guanacaste protege un mosaico de bosque seco, "
"humedales y costa."
msgstr ""
"The Guanacaste Conservation Area protects a mosaic of dry forest, wetlands "
"and coast."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2362
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2641
msgid "Se recorre en vehículo 4x4; los senderos de cada reserva son de tierra."
msgstr "It is explored by 4x4 vehicle; the trails in each reserve are dirt."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2363
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2642
msgid "https://whc.UNESCO.org/en/list/928/"
msgstr "https://whc.UNESCO.org/en/list/928/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2364
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2640
msgid ""
"La península de Nicoya es la mayor del país, con 3.200 km². Al norte el "
"bosque seco, al sur la selva húmeda y el Osa. El Área de Conservación "
"Guanacaste, creada en 1991, protege el norte de la península."
msgstr ""
"The Nicoya Peninsula is the largest in the country, at 3.200 km². To the "
"north, dry forest; to the south, rainforest and the Osa. The Guanacaste "
"Conservation Area, created in 1991, protects the northern part of the "
"peninsula."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2371
msgid ""
"La mayor selva primaria de las montanas centrales, con un río que la "
"atraviesa."
msgstr ""
"The largest primary forest in the central mountains, with a river running "
"through it."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2373
msgid ""
"Creado en 1978, protege la mayor selva primaria de las montanas centrales."
msgstr ""
"Created in 1978, it protects the largest primary forest in the central "
"mountains."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2374
msgid "Un solo sector del parque está abierto a los visitantes."
msgstr "Only one sector of the park is open to visitors."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2375
msgid "De 42.000 hectáreas, solo una parte pequeña recibe visitas."
msgstr "Of 42.000 hectares, only a small part receives visitors."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2376
msgid "El río Braulio Carrillo cruza el parque de lado a lado."
msgstr "The Braulio Carrillo River runs across the park from side to side."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2379
msgid "La harpía, ave de rapaz mayor, sobrevuela el dosel"
msgstr "The harpy eagle, the largest raptor, soars over the canopy"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2380
msgid "Ocelote y oso de anteojos en el suelo del bosque"
msgstr "Ocelot and spectacled bear on the forest floor"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2381
msgid "Mono aullador y perezoso de dos dedos"
msgstr "Howler monkey and two-toed sloth"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2382
msgid "Tucanes y pavas en el bosque de ribera"
msgstr "Toucans and peafowl in the riparian forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2385
msgid "Caminata guiada por el sendero del río Braulio Carrillo"
msgstr "Guided walk along the Braulio Carrillo River trail"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2386
msgid "Observación de aves con guía especialista"
msgstr "Birdwatching with a specialist guide"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2387
msgid "Visita al centro de interpretación del parque"
msgstr "Visit to the park's interpretation center"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2388
