"the mangroves."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2488
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2656
msgid ""
"El mirador se alcanza por sendero de tierra; el estero solo se visita en "
"bote."
msgstr ""
"The viewpoint is reached by a dirt trail; the estuary is only visited by "
"boat."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2490
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2655
msgid ""
"El parque protege el bosque seco que quedó entre el río Tárcoles y el "
"Pacífico. El mirador de la Piedra Bola ofrece la mejor vista del sector. El "
"río y los manglares se recorren en bote desde la entrada principal."
msgstr ""
"The park protects the dry forest left between the Tárcoles River and the "
"Pacific. The Piedra Bola viewpoint offers the best view of the area. The "
"river and the mangroves are explored by boat from the main entrance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2497
msgid ""
"Pueblo de surf con una playa protegida por el proyecto de tortugas Ostional."
msgstr "Surf town with a beach protected by the Ostional turtle project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2499
msgid "Pueblo de surf en la península de Nicoya, al norte de Guanacaste."
msgstr "Surf town on the Nicoya Peninsula, north of Guanacaste."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2500
msgid "Su playa de unos 1,4 km va del río Samara hasta el mar."
msgstr "Its 1.4 km beach runs from the Samara River to the sea."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2501
msgid "El estuario entre el Womble y el río atrae cientos de aves."
msgstr ""
"The estuary between the Womble and the river attracts hundreds of birds."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2502
msgid "Cerca están Isla Chora y la finca Rancho Quemado, con tortugas."
msgstr "Nearby are Isla Chora and the Rancho Quemado farm, with turtles."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2505
msgid "Tortuga verde anidando en la arena de la playa"
msgstr "Green turtle nesting in the beach sand"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2506
msgid "Mono aullador en el bosque seco cercano"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the nearby dry forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2508
msgid "Ara en los árboles del bosque seco"
msgstr "Macaw in the dry forest trees"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2511
msgid "Caminar por la playa durante la marea baja"
msgstr "Walk along the beach at low tide"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2512
msgid "Observación de aves en el estuario del río"
msgstr "Birdwatching at the river estuary"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2513
msgid "Recorrido de anidación de tortugas en Rancho Quemado"
msgstr "Turtle nesting tour at Rancho Quemado"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2514
msgid "Clase de surf para principiantes"
msgstr "Beginner surf lesson"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2517
msgid "La boca del río no es segura para nadar."
msgstr "The river mouth is not safe for swimming."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2518
msgid "La playa tiene corrientes fuertes y resacas."
msgstr "The beach has strong currents and rip tides."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2519
msgid "No deje sus pertenencias sobre la arena."
msgstr "Do not leave your belongings on the sand."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2521
msgid "Abierto todo el día"
msgstr "Open all day"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2522
msgid ""
"Sin entrada para la playa; el recorrido de tortugas tiene su propio precio"
msgstr "No beach entry fee; the turtle tour has its own price"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2523
msgid "Sector Ostional con unas 3.000 ha de playa y 2.700 ha marinas"
msgstr ""
"Ostional sector with about 3,000 ha of beach and 2,700 ha of marine waters"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2526
msgid "Bosque seco tropical, estuario de río y playa arenosa"
msgstr "Tropical dry forest, river estuary and sandy beach"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2527
msgid "0-30 msnm"
msgstr "0-30 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2529
msgid ""
"La playa protege los sitios de anidación de tortugas verdes dentro del "
"proyecto Ostional."
msgstr ""
"The beach protects the green turtle nesting sites within the Ostional "
"project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2530
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2661
msgid ""
"Se llega en bus o auto por carretera; la arena firme permite acceso a pie."
msgstr ""
"It is reached by bus or car by road; the firm sand allows access on foot."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2532
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2660
msgid ""
"Samara es un pueblo de surf en la península de Nicoya con playa de 1,4 km. "
"La entrada del río Samara forma un estuario con gran variedad de aves. La "
"playa forma parte del proyecto de tortugas Ostional."
msgstr ""
"Samara is a surf town on the Nicoya Peninsula with a 1.4 km beach. The mouth "
"of the Samara River forms an estuary with a wide variety of birds. The beach "
"is part of the Ostional turtle project."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2539
msgid "Puerto de entrada a la península de Osa y al parque nacional Corcovado."
msgstr "Gateway port to the Osa Peninsula and Corcovado National Park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2541
msgid "Principal puerto de acceso a la península de Osa y al parque Corcovado."
msgstr "Main access port to the Osa Peninsula and Corcovado National Park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2542
msgid "El pueblo se desarrollo con la creación del parque en 1963."
msgstr "The town grew with the creation of the park in 1963."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2543
msgid "La entrada principal del parque está a unos 10 km del centro."
msgstr "The main park entrance is about 10 km from the center."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2544
msgid "Hoy es la base de una gran cantidad de lodges de aventura."
msgstr "Today it is the base for a large number of adventure lodges."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2547
msgid "Ara escarlata en el dosel de la selva"
msgstr "Scarlet macaw in the rainforest canopy"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2548
msgid "Mono aullador en el bosque húmedo"
msgstr "Howler monkey in the humid forest"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2549
msgid "Tapir en los senderos del parque"
msgstr "Tapir on the park trails"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2550
msgid "Martin pescador a orillas del río Agujas"
msgstr "Kingfisher on the banks of the Agujas River"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2553
msgid "Visita al parque nacional Corcovado"
msgstr "Visit to Corcovado National Park"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2554
msgid "Paseo en bote por la Bahía de Drake"
msgstr "Boat ride through Drake Bay"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2555
msgid "Caminata sobre el manglar en Playa Juan Castillo"
msgstr "Walk on the mangroves at Playa Juan Castillo"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2556
msgid "Visita a los lodges de la zona"
msgstr "Visit to the lodges in the area"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2559
msgid "El camino al parque es de tierra y queda en mal estado."
msgstr "The road to the park is dirt and in poor condition."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2560
msgid "Reserve el permiso del parque y el guía con antelación."
msgstr "Book the park permit and guide in advance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2561
msgid "Lleve efectivo porque hay pocos cajeros."
msgstr "Bring cash because there are few ATMs."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2563
msgid "Todo el día; los cupos del parque se reservan con antelación"
msgstr "All day; park quotas are booked in advance"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2564
msgid "Sin entrada al pueblo; Corcovado exige permiso, guía y pago"
msgstr ""
"No fee to enter the town; Corcovado requires a permit, guide and payment"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2565
msgid "Pueblo costero con lodges, al norte de la península de Osa"
msgstr "Coastal town with lodges, north of the Osa Peninsula"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2568
msgid "Selva tropical húmeda y manglar costero"
msgstr "Humid tropical rainforest and coastal mangrove"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2569
msgid "0-50 msnm"
msgstr "0-50 masl"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2571
msgid ""
"Corcovado protege el bosque tropical húmedo más extenso del país y la vida "
"marina de Osa."
msgstr ""
"Corcovado protects the country's largest humid tropical forest and the "
"marine life of Osa."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2572
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2666
msgid ""
"El pueblo tiene calle principal pavimentada; el camino al parque es de "
"tierra y exige 4x4."
msgstr ""
"The town has a paved main street; the road to the park is dirt and requires "
"a 4x4."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2574
#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2665
msgid ""
"Puerto Jimenez es la principal puerta de entrada a la península de Osa. El "
"parque nacional Corcovado está a unos 10 km del pueblo. Al sur comienza la "
"Bahía de Drake y su reserva marina."
msgstr ""
"Puerto Jimenez is the main gateway to the Osa Peninsula. Corcovado National "
"Park is about 10 km from the town. To the south begins Drake Bay and its "
"marine reserve."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2670
msgid ""
"El Arenal es un estratovolcan de 1.670 msnm en el norte de Costa Rica. "
"Erupciono entre 1968 y 2010, con flujos de lava que brillaban de noche. La "
"colada de 1968 es hoy un sendero. El Observatorio Arenal está en la "
"carretera de subida."
msgstr ""
"Arenal is a 1,670 masl stratovolcano in northern Costa Rica. It erupted "
"between 1968 and 2010, with lava flows that glowed at night. The 1968 flow "
"is now a trail. Arenal Observatory is on the road up."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2671
msgid ""
"Se llega en vehículo hasta el mirador. El cráter se visita en vehículo "
"abierto. El clima es caluroso en la base."
msgstr ""
"You can drive as far as the viewpoint. The crater is visited in an open "
"vehicle. It is hot at the base."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2675
msgid ""
"Tortuguero es un parque de selva húmeda en la costa del Caribe. Solo se "
"llega en bote o en avión. Sus 31.187 hectáreas están cruzadas por canales y "
"el pueblo no tiene carreteras. Guarda la mayor playa de desove de tortuga "
"verde del hemisferio, de julio a octubre."
msgstr ""
"Tortuguero is a rainforest park on the Caribbean coast. It can only be "
"reached by boat or plane. Its 31,187 hectares are crisscrossed by canals and "
"the village has no roads. It holds the hemisphere's largest green turtle "
"nesting beach, from July to October."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2676
msgid ""
"No hay acceso por tierra: todo el recorrido es en bote y solo con guía. El "
"pueblo es plano pero la humedad es alta."
msgstr ""
"There is no road access: the whole route is by boat and only with a guide. "
"The village is flat but the humidity is high."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2680
msgid ""
"Manuel Antonio es el parque más visitado de Costa Rica. Es uno de los más "
"pequenos, con 1.983 hectáreas. Sus tres playas son Espadilla Sur, Manuel "
"Antonio y Puerto Escondido. Los monos carablanca y titi se ven en los "
"senderos y el parque cierra los lunes."
msgstr ""
"Manuel Antonio is the most visited park in Costa Rica. It is one of the "
"smallest, with 1,983 hectares. Its three beaches are Espadilla Sur, Manuel "
"Antonio and Puerto Escondido. White-faced capuchins and titi monkeys are "
"seen on the trails, and the park closes on Mondays."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2681
msgid ""
"Las playas son de arena y hay escalones en los accesos. El parque es "
"transitable a pie, pero con mucha gente."
msgstr ""
"The beaches are sandy and there are steps at the entrances. The park can be "
"walked, but it gets crowded."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2685
msgid ""
"Corcovado protege el mayor bosque primario que queda en el Pacífico de "
"Mesoamerica. Cubre 42.469 hectáreas. Reune las cuatro especies de monos del "
"país, junto con tapir, jaguar y puma. El ingreso es obligatorio con guía. Se "
"hace por las estaciones de Los Patos y Sirena."
msgstr ""
"Corcovado protects the largest primary forest left in Mesoamerica's Pacific. "
"It covers 42,469 hectares. It brings together the country's four monkey "
"species, along with tapir, jaguar and puma. A guide is mandatory. Entry is "
"through the Los Patos and Sirena ranger stations."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2686
msgid ""
"El acceso es en bote o a pie por senderos de tierra. El clima es caluroso y "
"húmedo todo el año."
msgstr ""
"Access is by boat or on foot along dirt trails. The climate is hot and humid "
"year round."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2690
msgid ""
"Rincón de la Vieja tiene nueve conos volcanicos. El Von Seebach es el más "
"alto, con 1.895 msnm. Fumarolas, ollas de barro hirviendo y la catarata La "
"Cangreja llenan el sector norte. Las termas del Río Clarillo son parte del "
"Área de Conservación Guanacaste. Es Patrimonio de la Humanidad de la UNESCO."
msgstr ""
"Rincón de la Vieja has nine volcanic cones. Von Seebach is the tallest, at "
"1,895 masl. Fumaroles, boiling mud pots and La Cangreja waterfall fill the "
"northern sector. The Río Clarillo hot springs are part of the Guanacaste "
"Conservation Area. It is a UNESCO World Heritage Site."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2691
msgid ""
"El sendero a la catarata es de tierra y se llega en vehículo. Las termas "
"tienen plataformas de descanso."
msgstr ""
"The trail to the waterfall is dirt and you can reach it by vehicle. The hot "
"springs have rest platforms."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2695
msgid ""
"Poás tiene uno de los crateres volcanicos más anchos del mundo. Su diametro "
"es de 1,3 km. La laguna del cráter cambia de color. La cima está a un corto "
"sendero desde el estacionamiento. Los gases son toxicos, por eso hay "
"barreras, y la visita exige reserva por turno."
msgstr ""
"Poás has one of the widest volcanic craters in the world. Its diameter is "
"1.3 km. The crater lagoon changes color. The summit is a short walk from the "
"parking lot. The gases are toxic, so there are barriers, and visits require "
"a timed reservation."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2696
msgid ""
"El mirador se alcanza sin esfuerzo. Hace frío y hay que subir de vuelta en "
"vehículo por la altura."
msgstr ""
"The viewpoint is reached with no effort. It is cold, and you have to drive "
"back up because of the altitude."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2700
msgid ""
"Irazú es el volcán más alto de Costa Rica, con 3.432 msnm. En días "
"despejados se ven los dos oceanos. La laguna del cráter cambia de color con "
"los minerales. La carretera llega cerca del cráter. La cima es fría y "
"ventosa todo el año."
msgstr ""
"Irazú is the tallest volcano in Costa Rica, at 3,432 masl. On clear days you "
"can see both oceans. The crater lagoon changes color with the minerals. The "
"road reaches close to the crater. The summit is cold and windy year round."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2701
msgid ""
"La carretera llega casi al cráter sin caminata. El frío y el viento hacen "
"que conviene bajar pronto."
msgstr ""
"The road reaches almost to the crater with no walking. The cold and wind "
"make it wise to head back down early."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2705
msgid ""
"Chirripó es el punto más alto de Costa Rica, con 3.820 msnm. Sus lagos "
"glaciares Ditkevi y Chadolin son la principal atracción. El amanecer sobre "
"el Pacífico completa el paisaje. El páramo está cubierto de frailejones y el "
"refugio se debe reservar con anticipacion."
msgstr ""
"Chirripó is the highest point in Costa Rica, at 3,820 masl. Its glacial "
"lakes Ditkevi and Chadolin are the main attraction. Sunrise over the Pacific "
"completes the landscape. The páramo is covered with frailejones and the "
"refuge must be booked in advance."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2706
msgid ""
"La subida toma dos días y el clima cambia muy rápido. Hace falta refugiarse "
"y llevar ropa de frío."
msgstr ""
"The climb takes two days and the weather changes very fast. You need to take "
"shelter and bring warm clothing."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2710
msgid ""
"Cahuita protege un arrecife de coral, una playa y un bosque de manglar. El "
"terremoto de 1991 levantó la costa y formo la playa actual. El arrecife está "
"bien conservado para el snorkel y un sendero de 8 km une la playa y el "
"bosque."
msgstr ""
"Cahuita protects a coral reef, a beach and a mangrove forest. The 1991 "
"earthquake uplifted the coast and formed the present beach. The reef is well "
"preserved for snorkeling, and an 8 km trail links the beach and the forest."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2711
msgid ""
"El sendero es de tierra y de tramo corto; el mar tiene corrientes y no hay "
"servicios dentro del parque."
msgstr ""
"The trail is a short dirt path; the sea has currents and there are no "
"services inside the park."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2715
msgid ""
"Marino Ballena protege 5.375 hectáreas, casi todas marinas, alrededor de la "
"península de Osa. Su tormbolo de arena parece una cola de ballena en marea "
"baja. Ballenas jorobadas de los dos hemisferios migran aqui y Uvita organiza "
"el festival de la ballena en temporada."
msgstr ""
"Marino Ballena protects 5,375 hectares, almost all of them marine, around "
"the Osa Peninsula. Its sandbar looks like a whale's tail at low tide. "
"Humpback whales from both hemispheres migrate here, and Uvita hosts the "
"whale festival in season."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2716
msgid ""
"El avistamiento se hace en lancha y el tormbolo se recorre a pie; no hay "
"acceso en silla de ruedas."
msgstr ""
"Whale watching is done by motorboat and the sandbar is walked on foot; there "
"is no wheelchair access."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2720
msgid ""
"Guayabo fue la ciudad precolombina más importante de Costa Rica, habitada "
"entre el 1000 a.C. y el 1400 d.C. Sus acueductos y tanques de piedra siguen "
"funcionando y las calzadas empedradas conectan los monticulos. Fue declarado "
"monumento nacional en 1973 y patrimonio de la ingenieria en 2009."
msgstr ""
"Guayabo was the most important pre-Columbian city in Costa Rica, inhabited "
"between 1000 BC and 1400 AD. Its aqueducts and stone tanks still work, and "
"the paved causeways connect the mounds. It was declared a national monument "
"in 1973 and a UNESCO engineering World Heritage Site in 2009."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2721
msgid ""
"El sendero principal es de tierra y es accesible en silla de ruedas; el "
"museo está a corta distancia."
msgstr ""
"The main trail is dirt and wheelchair accessible; the museum is a short "
"distance away."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2722
msgid "https://www.museosycostarica.go.cr/"
msgstr "https://www.museosycostarica.go.cr/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2725
msgid ""
"Tenorio tiene cuatro volcánes apagados y bosque nuboso con tapires y "
"quetzales. El Río Celeste se vuelve turquesa donde se mezclan dos ríos, "
"dentro del Área de Conservación Guanacaste. Un sendero de 3 km lleva a la "
"laguna azul, los tenideros y la catarata."
msgstr ""
"Tenorio has four dormant volcanoes and cloud forest with tapirs and "
"quetzals. The Río Celeste turns turquoise where two rivers meet, within the "
"Guanacaste Conservation Area. A 3 km trail leads to the blue lagoon, the "
"swimming pools and the waterfall."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2726
msgid ""
"El sendero es de tierra y empedrado con pendientes; hay que caminar entre "
"tres y cinco horas."
msgstr ""
"The trail is dirt and cobbled, with slopes; the walk takes between three and "
"five hours."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2730
msgid ""
"Palo Verde protege el humedal más importante de Costa Rica. Miles de aves "
"acuáticas migratorias, entre ellas los jabiru, pasan el invierno en sus "
"lagunas. Hay cocodrilos en las lagunas y el parque conserva uno de los "
"últimos bosques tropicales secos del país."
msgstr ""
"Palo Verde protects the most important wetland in Costa Rica. Thousands of "
"migratory waterbirds, including jabirus, spend the winter in its lagoons. "
"There are crocodiles in the lagoons and the park preserves one of the last "
"tropical dry forests in the country."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2731
msgid ""
"El recorrido principal es en lancha por las lagunas; el centro de visitantes "
"es accesible a pie."
msgstr ""
"The main tour is by motorboat through the lagoons; the visitor center is "
"accessible on foot."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2732
msgid "https://www.acguanacaste.ac.cr/"
msgstr "https://www.acguanacaste.ac.cr/"

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2735
msgid ""
"Isla del Coco está a 550 km de la costa y es Patrimonio de la Humanidad de "
"la UNESCO desde 1997. Concentra más de 400 especies endémicas de insectos y "
"plantas, ademas de cardumenes estacionales de tiburones martillo. El permiso "
"de acceso lo emite el parque."
msgstr ""
"Isla del Coco is 550 km off the coast and has been a UNESCO World Heritage "
"Site since 1997. It holds more than 400 endemic insect and plant species, "
"plus seasonal schools of hammerhead sharks. The park issues the access "
"permit."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2736
msgid ""
"Solo se llega en barco, con 36 horas de viaje; no hay ninguna facilidad en "
"la isla."
msgstr ""
"You can only get there by boat, with a 36-hour journey; the island has no "
"facilities at all."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2740
msgid ""
"Gandoca-Manzanillo protege manglares, un arrecife de coral y una playa de "
"arena de desove. La playa es sitio de anidación de tortuga baula, una de las "
"últimas poblaciones del Caribe. Un sendero costero une Manzanillo con la "
"laguna de Gandoca entre bosque de cativo y mangle rojo."
msgstr ""
"Gandoca-Manzanillo protects mangroves, a coral reef and a nesting beach. The "
"beach is a nesting site for the hawksbill turtle, one of the last "
"populations in the Caribbean. A coastal trail links Manzanillo with the "
"Gandoca lagoon through cativo forest and red mangrove."

#: includes/class-destination-spots.php:2741
msgid ""
"El sendero costero es de tierra y de clima caluroso; la playa es de arena "
"blanda y no tiene servicios."
msgstr ""
"The coastal trail is dirt and the climate is hot; the beach is soft sand and "
"has no services."

